# {version}

## Setup

### Bazel
```python
bazel_dep(name = "rules_req_compile", version = "{version}")
```

### PyPI
```bash
pip install req-compile=={version}
```

### Resolving inside Bazel

`req_compile_solver.wasm`, attached to this release, is `req-compile` as a WebAssembly module. The `requirements` extension runs it to resolve requirement files inside Bazel, without a host Python, when a `parse` tag sets `requirements_in`. Pin it in `MODULE.bazel`:
```python
http_file = use_repo_rule("@bazel_tools//tools/build_defs/repo:http.bzl", "http_file")
http_file(
    name = "req_compile_solver",
    sha256 = "{solver_sha256}",
    url = "https://github.com/periareon/req-compile/releases/download/{version}/req_compile_solver.wasm",
)
```
and pass `solver = "@req_compile_solver//file"` to the tag. Bazel needs `--experimental_repository_ctx_execute_wasm` (and, from Bazel 10, `--experimental_repository_ctx_wasm_compilation`); see `wasm/README.md`.

Additional documentation can be found at: https://github.com/periareon/req-compile
